SUMMARY:Deadline: Internet Society Fellowship Program 2027
DESCRIPTION:The Internet Society Fellowship supports people advancing Inter
 net connectivity\, policy or security in their communities. Fellows design
  and implement a practical project with deliverables such as policy briefs
 \, research reports\, training programs\, community engagement initiatives
 \, workshops or technical resources\, supported by a stipend of up to USD 
 5\,000\, a dedicated mentor\, weekly virtual...\n\nOrganisation: Internet 
 Society\nLocation: Remote\, worldwide\, with funded travel to one global o
 r regional Internet event. Requires continuous Internet access\, strong En
 glish\, and a passport valid at least six months beyond the anticipated tr
 avel.\nAward: Project stipend of up to USD 5\,000 (upon submission and app
 roval of the project budget)\, plus travel support to attend a global or r
 egional Internet event and a dedicated mentor aligned with the project are
 a. No application fee.\nDuration: 10 months (kick-off 22 February 2027\, g
 raduation early December 2027)\, including a six-month mentored project ex
 ecution period from 1 June to 30 November 2027. Minimum commitment of four
  hours per week.\n\nMore: https://www.internetsociety.org/fellowship/?utm_
 source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.internetsociety.org/fellowship/?utm_source=artificialnouvea
 ugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Remote\, worldwide\, with funded travel to one global or regional 
 Internet event. Requires continuous Internet access\, strong English\, and
  a passport valid at least six months beyond the anticipated travel.
END:VEVENT
